        "comments": "The assembly of Parablennius zvonimiri (fParZvo1) is based on 38X ONT data and 168X Arima Hi-C data generated as part of the ATLASea programme (https://www.atlasea.fr). The assembly process included the following steps: initial ONT assembly generation with Hifiasm, removal of contaminant sequences using Context, removal of haplotypic duplications using purge_dups, and Hi-C-based scaffolding with YaHS. No contigs were found to be contaminants (bacterial, archaeal, or viral). Additionally, 37 regions totaling 25.084 Mb (with the largest being 4.542 Mb) were identified as haplotypic duplications and removed. Finally, the primary assembly was analyzed and manually improved using Pretext. During manual curation, 3 haplotypic regions were removed, totaling 1.865Mb (with the largest being 1.318Mb). Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by Hi-C data were named in order of size.",
